<title>JAPAN: Swedish Export Credit launches 6.0% yen/A$ samurai.</title>
<headline>Swedish Export Credit launches 6.0% yen/A$ samurai.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish Export Credit Corp (SEK) on Monday launched 25 billion yen worth of 6.0 percent yen/Australian dual currency samurai bonds due on September 13, 1999, lead manager Daiwa Securities said.</p>
<p>The bonds will be priced at par.</p>
<p>The coupon will be paid in yen, while redemption will be in Australian dollars.</p>
<p>Holders of the samurai bonds will receive A$5,832.95 for each 500,000 yen bond held at maturity.  </p>
<p>The breakdown of the terms is as follows.</p>
<p> AMT 25 bln yen COUPON 6.0%	 MATURITY Sept 13, 1999</p>
<p> TYPE samurai   ISS PRICE 100 yen PAY DATE Sept 13, 1996</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD Aug 29 to Sept 12</p>
<p> INTEREST PAYMENT Sept 13 (annually)</p>
<p> LAST RATING AA+(S&amp;P), Aa3(Moody's)</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER Daiwa Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE Daiwa International Trust Bank</p>
</text>
